diff --git a/doc/man/man5/cgroup.conf.5 b/doc/man/man5/cgroup.conf.5
index 31cba7f..df6655a 100644
--- a/doc/man/man5/cgroup.conf.5
+++ b/doc/man/man5/cgroup.conf.5
@@ -97,6 +97,30 @@ enabled are io, pids, rdma, hugetlb and misc or all. If they do not exist in the
 system an error is logged. Only for cgroup/v2.
 .IP

+.TP
+\fBEnableTaskDelegation\fR=\fI<yes|no>\fR
+Allow tasks that explicitly request \fBSLURM_CGROUP_DELEGATE=memory\fR in
+their launch environment to manage memory cgroups below their Slurm task cgroup.
+The default is no. Requires cgroup/v2 and an available memory controller.
+Slurm keeps the task cgroup and its limits root-owned, creates a delegated
+subtree owned by the job user, and starts the task in its delegated/main leaf.
+Only the memory controller is delegated. Descendant cgroups remain subject to
+all ancestor limits, CPU affinity, and device restrictions.
+Slurm recursively tracks and removes descendants for opted-in tasks.
+Each task is limited to 258 descendants and a depth of 6 below its task cgroup.
+An invalid request or setup failure fails the task instead of granting partial
+delegation. This does not automatically impose a memory cap: the application
+must create a child cgroup, set memory.max (and memory.swap.max if appropriate),
+and move a new child process into it before that process allocates memory.
+For sibling survival after a child OOM, disable OOMKillStep for the step
+(e.g. srun --oom-kill-step=0). Slurm still reports descendant OOM events.
+Delegation is cooperative between processes sharing the job's Unix user ID;
+it does not isolate mutually untrusted processes with that same ID.
+Slurmd and slurmstepd must use matching patched binaries. Restart slurmd after
+installing them and enabling this option. Containerized tasks also need a
+writable view of their delegated subtree; this option does not alter mounts.
+.IP
+
 .SH "TASK/CGROUP PLUGIN"

 .LP
